@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Account and Worker Contact Role API
	Testing Koroneiki Account API functionality in relation to Worker Contact Roles.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Default Account Worker Role  |
	| Optional Account Worker Role |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary |
	| Koroneiki Engr Subsidiary |
	| Koroneiki Automotive      |
	| Koroneiki Engineering     |

Scenario: Assign account worker contact role to contact
	Koroneiki contacts should be able to be assigned to account worker contact roles on accounts.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Worker Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Worker                               |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                                  |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki     |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                             |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                     |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                             |
	| Region       | United States                            |
	| Status       | Approved                                 |
	| Tier         | Regular                                  |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              |
	And I assign worker contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles
	| Default Account Worker Role |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Default Account Worker Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Member"
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the worker contact role "Default Account Worker Role"
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the worker contact role "Member"

Scenario: Assign non existent account worker contact role to contact
	Koroneiki contacts should be able to be assigned to non existent account worker contact roles on accounts.

	Given I create a nested field for a nonexistent contact role with the following values
	| Description | This is the default worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Worker Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Worker                               |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a nested field for the worker contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the contact roles nested field value "${staticContactRolesNestedField}"
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                 | KORAUTO                              |
	| Contact Nested Field | ${staticContactsNestedField}         |
	| Description          | Test automotive account on koroneiki |
	| Fax Number           | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                 | Koroneiki Automotive                 |
	| Phone Number         | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Region               | United States                        |
	| Status               | Approved                             |
	| Tier                 | Regular                              |
	| Website              | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Default Account Worker Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Member"
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Worker Role" and the following values
	| Description | This is the default worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Worker Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Worker                               |
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the worker contact role "Default Account Worker Role"
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the worker contact role "Member"

Scenario: Assign non existent account worker contact role and account worker contact role to contact
	Koroneiki contacts should be able to be assigned to existent and non existent account worker contact roles on accounts.

	Given I create a nested field for a nonexistent contact role with the following values
	| Description | This is the default worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Worker Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Worker                               |
	And I rename the first contact role nested field variable
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the optional worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Optional Account Worker Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Worker                                |
	And I create a nested field for the contact role with the name "Optional Account Worker Role"
	And I rename the second contact role nested field variable
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a nested field for the worker contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the contact roles nested field value "${staticContactRolesNestedField1},${staticContactRolesNestedField2}"
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                 | KORAUTO                              |
	| Contact Nested Field | ${staticContactsNestedField}         |
	| Description          | Test automotive account on koroneiki |
	| Fax Number           | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                 | Koroneiki Automotive                 |
	| Phone Number         | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Region               | United States                        |
	| Status               | Approved                             |
	| Tier                 | Regular                              |
	| Website              | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Default Account Worker Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Optional Account Worker Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Member"
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Worker Role" and the following values
	| Description | This is the default worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Worker Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Worker                               |
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the worker contact role "Default Account Worker Role"
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the worker contact role "Optional Account Worker Role"
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the worker contact role "Member"

